## Control rule

Each phase has explicit inputs, outputs, success criteria, failure behavior, and
rollback. A later phase must not hide an incomplete earlier phase.

| Phase | Purpose | Success evidence | Failure behavior |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 Discover | Read-only inventory and collision/risk assessment | `discovery-inventory.json`, readiness report | Stop; no mutation |
| 1 Configure | Produce schema-valid `lz-config.json` | Schema and guard validation | Block export/render |
| 2 Render | Emit deterministic repository content | `render-manifest.json`, no unresolved tokens | Delete output and correct config |
| 3 Scaffold | Create/update target repository | Exact generated tree committed | Stop before settings/bootstrap |
| 4 Bootstrap | Reconcile Entra, GitHub, backend prerequisites | API read-back and identity inventory | Stop; preserve partial inventory |
| 5 Validate | Credential-free and read-only cloud checks | Required checks green | No apply |
| 6 Plan | Plan each active layer independently | Reviewed, non-destructive plans | Block approval |
| 7 Apply platform | Apply global/connectivity/management in order | State and health verification | Freeze affected layer |
| 8 Apply workloads | Apply selected workload/sandbox layers | Workload handoff evidence | Isolate failed layer |
| 9 Verify | Policy, diagnostics, backup, identity, cost validation | Acceptance report | Remediate before release |
| 10 Operate | Drift, patch, access, cost, incident cadences | Operational review records | Escalate overdue controls |
| 11 Upgrade | N-1 factory upgrade and layer plans | Upgrade evidence and clean drift | Roll back before unsafe apply |
| 12 Recover | State/service/regional recovery | Exercise or incident closure report | Maintain incident command |

